{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night","id":809881,"title":"New York by night","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-15T15:36:28-08:00","id":809881,"title":"New York by night","content":"My PCs are about to take a trip to NYC to learn more about a Belial's Brood coterie that started there. There are coming from Chicago and I'm using the Chicago sourcebook with Prince Maxwell and all that stuff. I want to show them that now, not two cities are quite the same and I was wondering about mood and theme for NYC. I discarded the Lancea Sanctum (NYC epitomizes the North not the Christian Belt), it's a modern city so not the the Circle, I want to show them something different so not the Invictus, NYC financial blood is Wall Street so not the Carthian Movement. Therefore I was thinking Ordo Dracul, it would make sense : the Defiants, building a new nation whatever it takes, spitting in the face of destiny and saying &quot;watch me&quot;.. So what would be your NYC in requiem ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T16:36:36-08:00","id":809916,"title":"","content":"I don't live in New York, so I'm not gonna give you any specific advice, just this one thing to consider: the Covenants in Requiem can, in fact, bear many faces. For example, the Circle doesn't have to be a bunch of nerds and neopagan weirdos, but stockbrokers, loan sharks and businesspeople that are so succesful thanks to the help of their spirits. The Invictus may be a street gang instead of a bunch of jaded old vamps in suits. The lancea can be crusaders, fighting crime on the street of Bronx. The Carthians may, for once, be in charge, but not as politicians, but trendsetters - hiding in plain sight, when every wannabe millionaire from Wall Streets wants to have their works of art, technology or whatever in their homes.<br /> <br /> There are dozens of options out there, shaped by the nature and, yes, soul of any given city.<br /> As for the Theme and Mood,.. I don't think a city as huge and diverse can really have these. They are more of a traits of your chronicle, so it largely depends on how you want to play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T16:58:42-08:00","id":809927,"title":"","content":"Well, for my group's setting of New York, it's so big that there's basically a couple domains throughout the city. In New York, the Invictus discard feudal practices of hierarchy and the like for a corporate identity. The Conspiracy of Silence is known to its Kindred as the Company, it's leadership form the Board, and its master is the Chairman. They use corporate lingo to disguise their activity, and manipulate a large number of proxies through actual corporate fronts.<br /> <br /> I was sort of inspired by the Board Meeting Elysium event in the supplement <i>Invite Only </i>which takes place in New York. I think the city is too big and weirdly balkanized for any one Kindred or even Covenant to claim domain over it, but you could have multiple claims and multiple territories.<br /> <br /> I'm from Manhattan and have spent most of my life in New York, so that informs my knowledge.<br /> <br /> I think New York certainly does have themes unique to it. While all cities are inevitably &quot;faster&quot; than living life around it, New York is pretty unique in the high energy that it exhibits. People are very busy, very stressed out, and always moving from one thing to the next. Time is valuable here. Incidentally, that's why it's been called the rudest city in the country.<br /> <br /> It's also very, very diverse, and you can have all sorts of interesting clashes between people of different cultural groups, different religious groups and others over the most incidental things. People with completely different experiences live right up next to one another, so those kinds of contrasts are really easily observed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:25:34-08:00","id":809987,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of New York City being overpopulated, yet so incredibly lonely as everybody unabashedly ignores one another. The streets are bustling, public transport is overcrowded, and traffic congestion is never-ending. Kindred are found everywhere in New York City, and yet they largely ignore one another's existences. It's mostly made up of disenfranchised, unaligned, rejected souls, notwithstanding any company. The small groups that do congregate can only rule small pieces of New York City (a building, a company, a street); the city is simply too competitive, diverse, and large in scope for any one Kindred or Covenant to control outright. The nits of Kindred that do get together pose as mortal gangs, church congregations, youth groups, boardroom executives, rarely do they overlap or associate with one another - the church goers and gang bangers stick to their own kind. Masquerade breaches, murder, gluttonous feeding, excessive embraces run amok in The Big Apple. Nobody exists to reign it in. Nobody to give a shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 01-15-2016, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T12:49:28-08:00","id":810326,"title":"","content":"I'm running in NYC and I'm from NYC. <br /> <br /> First thing you need to know is NYC is broken up into 5 boroughs. Each one was originally gonna be its own state because they are so large. Now I don't know if you wanna use what I've been doing but I broke NYC's Vampire community down into this. <br /> <br /> <br /> Manhattan = Invictus<br /> Brooklyn = Invictus / Circle of the Crone / Lancea et Sanctum<br /> Queens = Circle of the Crone<br /> Bronx = Carthian Movement<br /> Staten Island = Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> Each borough has it own prince and they come together in a counsel like the UN (Being the UN is in NYC) and deliberate different things. <br /> <br /> I think if I had to Give NYC over all a mood. Its Cold Fast and Weird. You can walk down a high tech street one moment and run into a street that is kept old for historical reasons. Train lines going anywhere you need and hidden night clubs. <br /> <br /> I thought it was be interesting to have Circle of the Crone have Queens under control and be at war with Brooklyn (Also Called Kings) <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://56.media.tumblr.com/43d5b0ea04d33a420c0437a6560648d8/tumblr_o12chs7LUi1rxzv9qo1_540.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T17:05:59-08:00","id":810405,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your inputs on the matter. That's an interesting idea: NYC is so big no one could claim Praxis over it. But my PCs are coming from Chicago, not a small town, if I play the &quot;too big city card&quot; it might give them the impression that their &quot;home city&quot; ain't that big and that NYC has specific problems due to its size that Chicago doesn't have. Do you think it's fair enough ? Or do you think that both cities are too large to be claimed by a single Prince ? BTW, I love the idea of each single borough being under a different influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T17:50:33-08:00","id":810419,"title":"","content":"Well currently had a ton of Violence going on so maybe you could play it up as Chicago does have a single prince but others are starting to wage a shadow war to kill that price and cut the city up. If the players help the prince it helps keep order and if they help the rebels it means more freedom but also chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T18:58:16-08:00","id":810445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night?p=810405#post810405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you all for your inputs on the matter. That's an interesting idea: NYC is so big no one could claim Praxis over it. But my PCs are coming from Chicago, not a small town, if I play the &quot;too big city card&quot; it might give them the impression that their &quot;home city&quot; ain't that big and that NYC has specific problems due to its size that Chicago doesn't have. Do you think it's fair enough ? Or do you think that both cities are too large to be claimed by a single Prince ? BTW, I love the idea of each single borough being under a different influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the thing to keep in mind is that Chicago's Kindred are concentrated in and around the loop, such that the person in charge of it effectively controls the Domain. That's part of how Maxwell derives his praxis. Because of the way the Boroughs are set up, I could easily see the resources being plentiful enough in different places that it's just not concentrated anywhere. It's like if there were like, two or three places like the Loop were everything is concentrated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T08:02:09-08:00","id":810625,"title":"","content":"OK, thanks you all and especially Leetsepeak: I'm working on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T18:25:24-08:00","id":810897,"title":"","content":"Sweet! Do let us know what you come up with, it's always really cool seeing the stuff that people make for their Domains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T19:20:06-08:00","id":810912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night?p=810445#post810445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the thing to keep in mind is that Chicago's Kindred are concentrated in and around the loop, such that the person in charge of it effectively controls the Domain. That's part of how Maxwell derives his praxis. Because of the way the Boroughs are set up, I could easily see the resources being plentiful enough in different places that it's just not concentrated anywhere. It's like if there were like, two or three places like the Loop were everything is concentrated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can easily take a feudal approach to ruling new york. Each of the 5 broughs will have a vassal &quot;baron&quot; who is in charge of that brough. All 5 barons will owe allegiance to the city prince (who has connections with the mayor and the city bureaucracy). You can then create drama when a baron challenges the prince and cuts off a whole brough to kindered loyal to the prince. Whoever controls the subway will have immense power and influence (sounds like a reasonable location for a Nosferatu elder/primogen to claim domain). Intra-clan/convent tension can be created if the broughs are not equally divided. Perhaps the Nosferatu lack a barony but instead forcefully took control of the subways. In this way all nosferatu, regardless of convent, see the subways as a safe home for their clan. One can do similar things with the Gangrel (maybe a gangrel elder controls the brox zoo, regardless of who the baron of the brox actually is) .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 01-17-2016, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T19:39:55-08:00","id":810923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night?p=810912#post810912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can easily take a feudal approach to ruling new york. Each of the 5 broughs will have a vassal &quot;baron&quot; who is in charge of that brough. All 5 barons will owe allegiance to the city prince (who has connections with the mayor and the city bureaucracy).</div> </div> </div> </div>You certainly could! I just thought not having a singular prince or unified hierarchy might help to highlight themes of cosmopolitan living, the sheer size and diversity of NYC, <i>and </i>help make it more unique from Chicago. <br /> <br /> That's definitely one way to do it, though you could make a lot of jokes about how there are much better people to &quot;befriend&quot; than the mayor of this mess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night?p=810912#post810912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You can then create drama when a baron challenges the prince and cuts off a whole brough to kindered loyal to the prince. Whoever controls the subway will have immense power and influence (sounds like a reasonable location for a Nosferatu elder/primogen to claim domain). Intra-clan/convent tension can be created if the broughs are not equally divided. Perhaps the Nosferatu lack a barony but instead forcefully took control of the subways. In this way all nosferatu, regardless of convent, see the subways as a safe home for their clan. One can do similar things with the Gangrel (maybe a gangrel elder controls the brox zoo, regardless of who the baron of the brox actually is) .</div> </div> </div> </div>The Clans in <i>Requiem </i>tend to not be that unified in outlook. I propose that New York further reinforces that because it's a city through which so many people move. You probably get a lot of Nomads passing through it as one of the bottlenecks of travel into the States from across the pond/other parts of the world, and lacking that lineage relation, they might be even less inclined to adopt a unified identity.<br /> <br /> This is all good stuff to consider though. There's a lot of different ways to execute a Kindred domain in New York while also paying mind to the city's potential themes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T19:45:36-08:00","id":810924,"title":"","content":"Its true that the clans in requiem tend not to be so unified but that isn't always the case. The 2e rulebook even has examples of cities where clan loyalty takes prominence over convent (if the convents even exist in a city). Alternatively, you can easily replace clan with convent in my post and the results will be the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T20:16:35-08:00","id":810933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night?p=810924#post810924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its true that the clans in requiem tend not to be so unified but that isn't always the case. The 2e rulebook even has examples of cities where clan loyalty takes prominence over convent (if the convents even exist in a city). Alternatively, you can easily replace clan with convent in my post and the results will be the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware, hence my suggestion that the reason why New York is even less likely to produce strong clan based loyalty is the larger amount of Kindred, and the likely larger amount of Nomads passing through. This also dovetails nicely with the noted phenomenon of how people feel paradoxically more alone in New York than they do in a small town in the middle of nowhere, because at least people in that town care that you're there (for better or worse) while in a city of millions, you're just another pair of feet in the crowd.<br /> <br /> Basically, I feel that there's a more compelling case to be made for it being notably absent in New York City specifically, though your mileage may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T20:23:19-08:00","id":810937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night#post809881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My PCs are about to take a trip to NYC to learn more about a Belial's Brood coterie that started there. There are coming from Chicago and I'm using the Chicago sourcebook with Prince Maxwell and all that stuff. I want to show them that now, not two cities are quite the same and I was wondering about mood and theme for NYC. I discarded the Lancea Sanctum (NYC epitomizes the North not the Christian Belt), it's a modern city so not the the Circle, I want to show them something different so not the Invictus, NYC financial blood is Wall Street so not the Carthian Movement. Therefore I was thinking Ordo Dracul, it would make sense : the Defiants, building a new nation whatever it takes, spitting in the face of destiny and saying &quot;watch me&quot;.. So what would be your NYC in requiem ?</div> </div> </div> </div>In NYC you don't have to throw away &quot;The Lancea et Sanctum&quot; have them just like the churches in NYC pockets all over the place but not having complete control over an area. You could play with the idea of they have power by having so many pockets.<br /> <br /> <br /> With how I have the city set up each each borough controlled by a different covenant who has over all control in a area but allows other covenants to have space in there territory. Allowing them to do there practices but you are subject to rules from the controlling powers in the area.<br /> <br /> Also for by having each borough controlled by a different covenant you can have political parties visiting each other territories. Then also I have the covenants meet together in a counsel meeting like the U.N to talk of what is best for the kindred of NYC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T00:58:30-08:00","id":811029,"title":"","content":"I will have the borough approach, since it's just a trip, I'm going to come up with a dozen of vampires and, most importantly a theme and a mood for each borough. I like the idea of different princes gathering once in a while for a Conclave and, possibly, unbound territories which, on paper are the province of a Prince, but which actually are left untended because you can't lord over everything. Nomads are a good idea too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T08:51:08-08:00","id":811147,"title":"","content":"I'm not done yet, but that's the first draft.<br /> <br /> New York general mood<br /> <br /> The basic idea is that the city is way too large to be claimed by a single kindred. NYC has five boroughs which loosely correspond to the various kindred influence. Each borough is under a different influence and the five leaders hold a conclave at least once a year to address potential threats and common issues.<br /> Anyway, even broken down into five boroughs no Prince can claim he controls everything that's going on in his own domain: a lot of districts remain unwatchable, whole parts of the city are occupied by nomads, unbound or even small covenants which practices and traditions totally degenerated. <br /> <br /> That's the general idea, specifics vary from one borough to another. I'll start with Staten Island.<br /> <br /> Staten Island:<br /> <br /> A rural part of NYC till the 60's, Staten Island is the less populated of the 5 boroughs (over 470 000 inhabitants though), after urbanization soared, concerns about preserving the old rural parts of the island rose as well, leading to a policy preserving the local ecology: parks, zoos etc. Close to 80% of the population is white and it is the only borough in NYC where the Republican Party generally beats the Democrats.<br /> <br /> The mood of the kindred side of Staten Island is an old Victorian mood, a part of NYC that seems being a remanent of the 19th century. Very conservative and quite isolationist the Island is under a double influence. First and foremost the Ordo Dracul whose Society for sciences is a front office for managing and funding their real experiments. Secondly the Lancea Sanctum rules over the Roman Catholic Church and warn their flock against these secular and blasphemous scientists whose soulless science is an outrage in the face of God. Needless to say the opposition between both covenants has been fierce since the start and has led to many conflicts a lot of them vicious and deadly. <br /> <br /> Staten Island's Lancea Sanctum is very traditional we might even risk the word &quot;bigotry&quot; to qualify it. Meaning gaining high status in the covenant is about being devout to the words of Longinus and therefore (they think) excelling at handling Theban Sorcery. The politicial and organizational aspects of the covenant are a secular necessity but brings little prestige. Quite ironically it's very similar to the way the Defiants consider their own politicians, including their Kogaion.<br /> <br /> Several decades ago that led to a surprising result: Sanctified and Defiant politicians came together to try to put an end to the constant and counterproductive infightings between the two covenants. At first the coterie they formed was met with scorn and mockery but the truth is they had two assets none of the two covenants could ignore. First they really had secular power: you might consider that only science or theology matters but you'll need infrastructure, funding and many secular/mundane concerns being taking care of in order to carry on. Second they really are politicians and thus they are able to add some water to their wine and, by giving some ground, actually achieving something. And achieving they did, the Council (the name of their coterie) has greatly eased the coexistence of the two covenants. It's not easy, they don't have the highest status in their respective covenants and have to be clever and subtle when they are pulling their strings, negotiations can be going for month for petty details considered highly symbolic for one or both (the worse case scenario) covenants and crucial but down to earth issues might be dealt with in one night by high status Sanctified and Defiant alike unconcerned by such mundane questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","user":"JPS","date":". 01-18-2016, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T10:12:33-08:00","id":811184,"title":"","content":"Manhattan <br /> <br /> For most non New Yorker kindred, Manhattan seems to epitomize everything the Invictus crave for: money and power worldwide. And it did for those British Invictus who first ruled Long Island especially when it became the British center of operations during the independence war. The American Invictus love to remind everybody of the crucial part they played during those nights, rising against the British presence through the gangs and militia they controlled and being the cornerstone in the victory against the British vampires when George Washington freed the city in 1783. Some might say that patriotism had little to do with that, they'll add that younger Invictus saw an opportunity to seize power from their elders and they took it. Anyway in the meantime, the Circle of the Crone played a clever game. The Circle knew too well that even in the New World , even when fleeing persecution with other persecuted minorities, those former minorities would become the new orthodoxy and would in return persecute pagans and put them to the stake just as the Europeans did to them not that long ago. And it wouldn't concern only the kine: taking advantage of the bigotry of the time, the British Lancea Sanctum allied with the British Invictus would bully the Circle itself. And now what ? What they gonna do ? Wait to see if the American Invictus would be more charitable ? The acolytes knew they won't. So they took matters into their own hands, as the British influence natural and supernatural alike was fading, they used sorcery, shamanism and voodoo rituals to fill the empty space, to seize control of the economic and financial powers. Never ever again, the Circle will be oppressed because they learnt their lesson well: no matter who you are, no matter how you used to be persecuted in the past, if you control businesses, banks, politicians everybody and his dog would legitimate you. And that's what they did, let the Invictus upstarts and the American Firebrands win the vampiric side of the independence war, in the meantime the Acolytes would spread their grasp on finance and industry through magic and pacts.<br /> <br /> So here we are today: the Invictus is known as the Syndicate, ruling the gangs and especially organized crime. They thought they could take control of big money after the independence war but it was to late: when it was all set and done, the Circle of the Crone was the unmitigated ruler of what would become Wall Street. Now they call their organization the Firm. Forget about your neopagan hippies, we are talking suits, corporation boards, the banking system, the Federal Reserve, traders, raiders, banksters. You want to rise in the business ? You'll have to cheat your way to the top, you'll have to strike a deal with the Firm. Rituals are not cheap bacchanals conducted in some exclusive pub in the neighborhood it's been performed in back office, in secret corporate rooms with velvet curtains, marble columns and several millions worth occult paraphernalia.<br /> <br /> (Thanks Woland)<br /> <br /> Now the Executive Board rules the city. The Prince (known as the Chairman) is from the Firm (Circle of the Crone) and the board is a collegial representation of the Firm and the Syndicate. The Lancea Sanctum, the Movement and Ordo Dracul aren't represented. Nonetheless the Lancea Sanctum holds sway on the Syndicate (whose Godfather has a strong Italian legacy). The few Ordo Dracul just don't care ; as for the Firebrands they are just pissed off about having being played upon and discarded from the political arena although they also played a key role in the &quot;battle of New York&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","user":"JPS","date":". 01-18-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T12:16:24-08:00","id":811250,"title":"","content":"The Bronx<br /> <br /> In the old days, the Bronx history mixed with Manhattan's but when talking about modern history you'll have to consider two eras: pre and post the 90's zero tolerance policy. Before the 90's the situation spiraled totally out of control. The place was such an urban jungle and the most infamous crime plagued place in the US that even the kindred counterpart of the borough was dangerous. We're talking ruthless nomads, diablerist coteries, lunatic kindred and forbidden covenants such as the Brood or any kind of degenerated self appointed guru kindred rising star. So when the kindred say the &quot;Carthian Movement used to be charge&quot; it has to be taken with a grain of salt to say the least. Sure they were the only traditional covenant around, but they were battling constantly and we are not talking about some political backstabbing subtleties, we are talking guns and fangs, we are talking torpor and final death, we are talking no rules at all.<br /> <br /> Then surely what had to happen happened: kine and kindred alike grew tired of the whole mess that threatened to spill over Manhattan itself. They decided it was time to step in and it backfired dramatically. The humans call it the zero tolerance policy and it was, indeed, the mortal counterpart of this war. For the kindred it was a full fledged war: as the police forces were taking the streets back by day, by night the Syndicate maimed, burnt, staked, tortured or otherwise introduced to the sunrise every kindred judged suspicious or simply poor suckers they didn't know. They probably killed many innocent leeches (if there is such a thing) but no mofo that crossed their path ever survived the experience. Okay I know what you're thinking: the Carthians allowed it ? They left the Invictus seize whole districts in the Bronx ? Actually they had little choices, they couldn't wage a two front war. Battles against the unbound (one might say the unleashed) had left a bitter taste and personal feuds blinded them all ; the Syndicate, at the time, looked like the lesser evil. Fools they were. When the unbound kindred were burn to the ground what do you think happened ? The Syndicate took credit for it all claiming the Bronx although they had only one third of it. Obviously they had the nicest parts, those parts in which gentrification began and guess what ? The Firm backed them: the Godfather was declared Capo of the Bronx and the Firebrands were discarded once again: they won't be represented in any Conclave because for most kindred from other boroughs, the Bronx is a natural (geographically speaking) extension of Manhattan. So of course, the Carthians do have a &quot;Prince&quot; (they call him Leader) but he's not recognized anywhere, he could as well being a tribal chief. Too much is too much. The Movement lost Manhattan in the 18th century and now the Bronx ; although they paid more than their share to win these battles, although they're still holding power on most of the Bronx, they're still being denied. Now this is war. The Firebrands are, indeed, branding fire. Don't go north Bronx today because the old days are back: violence, crime, ruthless gangs and crazy kindred, the Firebrands will open the very gates of hell to bring both the Syndicate and the Firm screaming and kicking to hell. That's a nasty war, if you're not a Carthian and you're strolling north the Bronx you might end up dead, if you're foolish enough to claim some Syndicate or Firm support you will be killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T14:50:53-08:00","id":811335,"title":"","content":"Brooklyn<br /> <br /> In recent history Brooklyn has become the third business center in NYC after two Manhattan's districts. The theme of Brooklyn is new blood. An Invictus covenant, totally disconnected from the Syndicate did a lot of work to propel Brooklyn into the business competition. They didn't do that alone though, they're working with the Movement to smooth employers-employees relationships and it is working. What happened ? New blood happened, neonates and some ancillae are managing the place. Historically speaking places of power in NYC were about Long Island, the oldest vampires struggled there. Okay there's the exception of Staten Island that drew some old vampires too, but the Richmond County has always been about ideological feuds, science versus religion, the Lancea Sanctum against the Ordo Dracul, secular power never mattered that much for Staten Island's kindred. Now, in Brooklyn we're talking business. We are talking ambitious young vampires that left Manhattan for Brooklyn to start something there because they couldn't compete with Manhattan's elders. The most dynamic, daredevil and ingenious neonates started to emulate American pioneers: building a new world, fleeing the old world to start again. Okay that might sound a bit emphatic since no Brooklyn kindred ever crossed the Atlantic Ocean but in their mind it was the same thing, in their mind the Syndicate battling against the British is a big joke: most Syndicate leaders are actually Europeans, some them even British. In their mind they fled from the old world (Manhattan) where the game was rigged for neonates and they carved their own destiny like mortals did in 1776.<br /> <br /> As a result Brooklyn &quot;by night&quot; can be quite a sight for a non New Yorker kindred: the borough is being held by young vampires. Ancillae are the eldest and they are few of them. Younger vampires also means closer to the Man and Brooklyn kindred are probably much more attuned to mortals than those from Manhattan. You'll have the stereotypes alright: Invictus is opposed to the Movement, Lancea Sanctum is close to the Invictus and the Circle's Acolytes are kinda blasphemous to the Sanctified. It's just that they won't take all these things to the extent oldest kindred do. They won't kill each other over this, they won't deny their rights to be represented over this. Don't kid yourself, they're still vampires and they can be vicious to one another but it's generally for personal matters. As a community though, it's working and the borough is a rising star, still way behind Manhattan so their Elders don't see them as a threat ... yet.<br /> <br /> What's striking about the Brooklyn's kindred is their urge to belong. For instance: Brooklyn's Invictus don't call themselves the Syndicate, the Corporation or anything along those lines, they call themselves Invictus and they try to emulate them in any way: the titles, the courtesy, the way they dress. Some old fashioned old world leeches might call them wannabes but are they ? In some ways they are closer to the traditional Invictus than the Syndicate, it's just they are much younger. And this is their strength: they might appeal to gifted neonates feeling that they can achieve in Brooklyn what they would be denied in other cities. The same could be said about the the Movement: these Firebrands talk about socialism, equal standard of livings, about being the 99%. But they're still close to mortals and improving social daily conditions still matters to them and they're able to deal on regular basis with the Invictus to achieve what they want. To them the Bronx's Carthians are bogeymen lost to the cause, they won't have anything to do with them and are glad they are not represented in the Conclave. The same thing goes with the Lancea Sanctum: they're here to torment mortals but especially the evil ones and, amazingly enough they generally lean towards the Movement, explaining to the Invictus that Christian charity commands that they should be charitable with those less fortunate and lenient towards the poor. The result is that the Lancea Sanctum in Brooklyn is greatly smoothing things up between the Carthians and the Invictus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T15:44:16-08:00","id":811354,"title":"","content":"And that's what I did for Queens<br /> <br /> The Queens<br /> <br /> The Queens is the most multi cultural borough in NYC, it used to be the movie capital of the nation before the industry moved to Hollywood, nonetheless it's still an artistic cluster: movie studios, theaters, museums, the Queens is vibrating with art. <br /> <br /> So what's happening in the kindred world ? Which covenant claims the Queens as a domain ? The truth is: none. Sure you'll have companies, night clubs run by the Invictus, you'll have a light version (a more liberal version) of the Lancea Sanctum, the Movement will be outspoken about gay rights, pro choice and political correctness. The Circle of the Crone will fight for neopagan rights and spread the witchcraft culture and the Ordo Dracul, well, they would migrate to Staten Island unless they're dealing with plastic surgery. Everyone can belong in the Queens but none nearly fits like the Daeva do. <br /> <br /> Yeah, you got that right: no covenant can claim the Queens, but a clan does. The sirens are everywhere: Invictus Daeva might run this night club or art gallery, Firebrand Daeva might be quite convincing about the new social political trends, Lancea Sanctum Daeva might urge revisiting the dogma to fit the modern world and Ordo Dracul Daeva might long for circumventing the curse to help her being more proficient at socializing. They might be everywhere but, at the end the night, they'll throw parties, talk about art and the hottest things, they'll decide about who's talented and who's not, which political thoughts are trendy and who's in and who's out in the kindred political game. They really run the show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T22:11:40-08:00","id":813178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night?p=811250#post811250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bronx<br /> <br /> In the old days, the Bronx history mixed with Manhattan's but when talking about modern history you'll have to consider two eras: pre and post the 90's zero tolerance policy. Before the 90's the situation spiraled totally out of control. The place was such an urban jungle and the most infamous crime plagued place in the US that even the kindred counterpart of the borough was dangerous. We're talking ruthless nomads, diablerist coteries, lunatic kindred and forbidden covenants such as the Brood or any kind of degenerated self appointed guru kindred rising star. So when the kindred say the &quot;Carthian Movement used to be charge&quot; it has to be taken with a grain of salt to say the least. Sure they were the only traditional covenant around, but they were battling constantly and we are not talking about some political backstabbing subtleties, we are talking guns and fangs, we are talking torpor and final death, we are talking no rules at all.<br /> <br /> Then surely what had to happen happened: kine and kindred alike grew tired of the whole mess that threatened to spill over Manhattan itself. They decided it was time to step in and it backfired dramatically. The humans call it the zero tolerance policy and it was, indeed, the mortal counterpart of this war. For the kindred it was a full fledged war: as the police forces were taking the streets back by day, by night the Syndicate maimed, burnt, staked, tortured or otherwise introduced to the sunrise every kindred judged suspicious or simply poor suckers they didn't know. They probably killed many innocent leeches (if there is such a thing) but no mofo that crossed their path ever survived the experience. Okay I know what you're thinking: the Carthians allowed it ? They left the Invictus seize whole districts in the Bronx ? Actually they had little choices, they couldn't wage a two front war. Battles against the unbound (one might say the unleashed) had left a bitter taste and personal feuds blinded them all ; the Syndicate, at the time, looked like the lesser evil. Fools they were. When the unbound kindred were burn to the ground what do you think happened ? The Syndicate took credit for it all claiming the Bronx although they had only one third of it. Obviously they had the nicest parts, those parts in which gentrification began and guess what ? The Firm backed them: the Godfather was declared Capo of the Bronx and the Firebrands were discarded once again: they won't be represented in any Conclave because for most kindred from other boroughs, the Bronx is a natural (geographically speaking) extension of Manhattan. So of course, the Carthians do have a &quot;Prince&quot; (they call him Leader) but he's not recognized anywhere, he could as well being a tribal chief. Too much is too much. The Movement lost Manhattan in the 18th century and now the Bronx ; although they paid more than their share to win these battles, although they're still holding power on most of the Bronx, they're still being denied. Now this is war. The Firebrands are, indeed, branding fire. Don't go north Bronx today because the old days are back: violence, crime, ruthless gangs and crazy kindred, the Firebrands will open the very gates of hell to bring both the Syndicate and the Firm screaming and kicking to hell. That's a nasty war, if you're not a Carthian and you're strolling north the Bronx you might end up dead, if you're foolish enough to claim some Syndicate or Firm support you will be killed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find it interesting you made the north bronx seem very violent when most of the time its the south Bronx that's more insane. Imagine all the things happening in the projects that no one see's.<br /> <br /> The Bronx gets even more interesting the father in the past you go. You know the really rich use the live in the Bronx and the poor lived in Manhattan. <br /> <br /> Also the has I believe the largest cemetery on the east coast. A few people who live by it told me the homeless live in the catacombs bellow it. Calling it the 4 corners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 01-21-2016, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T09:24:55-08:00","id":813425,"title":"","content":"Interesting info about the catacombs. To be honest with you the north and south Bronx was a geographic matter, I pictured the Invictus coming from Manhattan and retaking parts of the Bronx block by block. So do you think that considering violence is sweeping over northern Bronx should have a special treatment ? I mean I was picturing the cliches: gangs, drugs, crack houses and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T14:08:36-08:00","id":813635,"title":"","content":"I've actually been going through the published fiction and setting fluff for CoD and compiling a list of all the bits and pieces that I can pin down geographically. It's pretty incomplete, but so far I know there's a fiction bit called &quot;Nightmare Wave&quot; in <i>Daeva: Kiss of the Succubus</i> which refers to events in New York (specifically some sort of blood sympathy backlash that affected New York kindred with &quot;relatives&quot; in New Orleans after Katrina), as well as a short blurb in <i>Damnation City</i>. If you have either of these books, you may be interested in looking at them for inspiration.<br /> <br /> There's also a fiction bit in <i>Gangrel: Savage and Macabre</i> called &quot;Witches, Kisses, and Bombs&quot; which refers to &quot;the Tombs&quot; about a dozen blocks away from either 5th or 7th street (can't recall which), which is roughly geographically accurate for the Manhattan Detention Complex. It also makes reference to seeing a fire in the direction of &quot;the stockyards,&quot; however, which as far as I know doesn't make sense if the story's taking place in Manhattan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:11:01-08:00","id":813726,"title":"","content":"The Tombs is a nickname for the detention complex, nothing special really.<br /> <br /> It sucks if you have to spend the night there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T20:18:32-08:00","id":813871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night?p=813726#post813726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tombs is a nickname for the detention complex, nothing special really.<br /> <br /> It sucks if you have to spend the night there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that; sorry if I wasn't clear. I brought it up because some evidence led me to suspect that the story in question was taking place in Manhattan, but other evidence seemed to exclude that possibility. Unless there's a &quot;the Tombs&quot; in another major urban area in the US, I suspect that the story took place in a fictional city, which wouldn't be all that unusual for <i>Requiem </i>fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T21:19:58-08:00","id":813898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night?p=813635#post813635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've actually been going through the published fiction and setting fluff for CoD and compiling a list of all the bits and pieces that I can pin down geographically. It's pretty incomplete, but so far I know there's a fiction bit called &quot;Nightmare Wave&quot; in <i>Daeva: Kiss of the Succubus</i> which refers to events in New York (specifically some sort of blood sympathy backlash that affected New York kindred with &quot;relatives&quot; in New Orleans after Katrina), as well as a short blurb in <i>Damnation City</i>. If you have either of these books, you may be interested in looking at them for inspiration.<br /> <br /> There's also a fiction bit in <i>Gangrel: Savage and Macabre</i> called &quot;Witches, Kisses, and Bombs&quot; which refers to &quot;the Tombs&quot; about a dozen blocks away from either 5th or 7th street (can't recall which), which is roughly geographically accurate for the Manhattan Detention Complex. It also makes reference to seeing a fire in the direction of &quot;the stockyards,&quot; however, which as far as I know doesn't make sense if the story's taking place in Manhattan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do, I'll have a look, thanks for the tip <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T07:54:03-08:00","id":814125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night?p=813425#post813425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting info about the catacombs. To be honest with you the north and south Bronx was a geographic matter, I pictured the Invictus coming from Manhattan and retaking parts of the Bronx block by block. So do you think that considering violence is sweeping over northern Bronx should have a special treatment ? I mean I was picturing the cliches: gangs, drugs, crack houses and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea the crack houses and stuff are more to the south Bronx. The closer you get to the area near Rikers Island the more you see gang, drugs, crack houes and the like. You could always do this. The Invictus are taking back parts of the Bronx because some of there elders are in torpor there. In the north Bronx you get less projects and it seem more suburban than urban but yes here there are gangs mostly held up in homes rather than projects.<br /> <br /> Also in the south Bronx there is enough people doing voodoo and there odd things. The police in some of these areas have to know what different things mean. Like what nailing a tongue to a tree near someones house means.<br /> <br /> Oh also Yankee Stadium is in the south Bronx.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 01-22-2016, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T12:00:17-08:00","id":814962,"title":"","content":"I know there's the temptation to make things darker, and it's also a sort of natural extension of adding supernatural creatures into the already complicated situation of New York City, but don't lose sight of the fact that it's safer than it's ever been. Even if that's not necessarily true in your Chronicles of Darkness, it might be that this idea of New York as a &quot;tamed city&quot; that's gentrifying a la parts of Brooklyn and Manhattan (I've heard that it's beginning to happen in the south bronx too, but I rarely have a reason to go there) is more powerful than the reality, and that could introduce complications into your gameplay.<br /> <br /> Like for example, Manhattan is just NOT the place to be getting into big fights in the streets. It's too crowded and the police will be on you even if you flee the scene. In that vein, the Kindred that live there might be very harsh in their enforcement of the Masquerade. It's not that they're afraid of people thinking Vampires exist, but rather that they don't want people to realize how unsafe they are walking the streets, because they think the gangbangers and muggers are in other boroughs.<br /> <br /> Just some food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T02:35:44-08:00","id":815327,"title":"","content":"I liked the idea of the Firebrands being pissed off in the Bronx but I'll move them south <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As for the old days being back I'll have to come up with something, perhaps an increase in gang activity, nowhere near it used to be but enough to be of concern for the Police, I'll have to work on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:10:46-08:00","id":816377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809881-new-york-by-night?p=815327#post815327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the idea of the Firebrands being pissed off in the Bronx but I'll move them south <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As for the old days being back I'll have to come up with something, perhaps an increase in gang activity, nowhere near it used to be but enough to be of concern for the Police, I'll have to work on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want something more contemporary, you could focus on the fact that New York is a magnet for terror threats, the NYPD, already a vast force that outnumbers the militaries of several nations has ramped up its presence on the street and the force it brings to bear against suspects, and that these things have consequences by way of escalation. Terror threats and a backlash against an increasingly militarized police force are already a powder keg of tension without relying on an idea of New York that died with the 1980s.<br /> <br /> Gang violence is still a problem, but even the worst parts of New York don't really carry the weight of a place like say, Chicago. There's definitely tension there though. Look back at what I said about the intensity of life in New York City, then combine it (at least, for certain segments of the population) with existential fear regarding figures of authority and serious doubts about their capacity to actually protect communities. It makes living in the city very stressful, even without the L train being shut down for a few years or the rent for your apartment skyrocketing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T10:50:17-08:00","id":816987,"title":"","content":"Ok I reorganized that: the Firebrands tried to raise hell again in the Bronx in the mid 90s but it was a failure since the authorities retaliated immediately and forcefully. Then the day came: on 9/11 they saw the collapse of the Twin Towers and they knew right away which gates of which hell they would open. Saying that the Bronx' Firebrands are radicals is a vast understatement. They're trying to infiltrate or to create potential terrorists and use them against their enemies. They wished 9/11 had happened by night, but it wouldn't had made any sense for mortals, right ? Obviously, most terror threats don't originate from the Carthians but they managed to trigger a dozen of them and, on a couple of occasions, they actually pulled it off. Now the Syndicate and the Firm know what they are up to, they know the terror threats ain't only natural origin but supernatural as well. They're out to get every last of them but Carthians changed their MO: they're mostly hiding, going out only in bands of 5 or 6 at least, they're gathering networks of potential terrorists and they are not picky about them: Muslim fanatics, communist terrorist cells, far right radicals willing to take the government down. They'll all do if they have the nerves, anyway the Carthians don't care about these mortal's petty ideologies. It's irrelevant: they'll be manipulated into suicidal missions to get to their enemies. The Firm and the Syndicate are extremely concerned, their worst nightmare being a successful infiltration of their organization by those mad Firebrands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T11:55:31-08:00","id":817038,"title":"","content":"I started writing an NYC setting last year, though I ended up largely ignoring it for the past year as my work situation got complicated. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/412051-new-york-by-night\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-york-by-night</a><br /> <br /> I basically created the setting as &quot;The Night Cities&quot; which included the New Jersey region (Jersey City, Hoboken and surrounding towns) across the Hudson from Manhattan. Essentially a highly political member of the Lancea Sanctum claimed the title of Prince-Archbishop of Manhattan, and claims praxis over the rest of the City, the other boroughs and Jersey City/Hoboken region each have a Prince but none of them would ever dare use that title out of respect for the Prince-Archbishop.<br /> <br /> I find the idea that NYC as a political entity, is almost impossible to administer from a Kindred perspective fascinating. I also like the idea that, the elder Kindred have largely established their domains decades ago, and often become attached to ethnic enclaves which exist around the City moreso than specific covenants. This leads to a large number of 50 to 100 year old Ancillae who largely fight to get the patronage of certain elders in their attempts to help their specific covenant gain the upper hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5106-umoja","name":"Umoja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:54:10-08:00","id":820396,"title":"","content":"Thanks Umoja, I had a look and it's nice. My setting is pretty advanced now and I have to integrate that Brood of Belial (which will be set on Staten Island) so I'm keeping my version. We played last Friday Night they ended up being &quot;interviewed&quot; by the Firm and the Syndicate and they got accepted in the city: when the authorities heard that the Belial cell that plagued Staten Island operates now in Chicago and might still have a NYC based center, they were obviously interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}